Host pad source: the state of the PS2 controllers comes from the embedding program, not from raylib

What it fixes: the pad state reached the guest only through raylib (IsKeyDown, IsGamepad*, axis reads)
and the runtime knew exactly 2 ports with 1 slot each. A host that owns its window and input (SDL3)
needs to feed the pads itself, with its own mapping, with up to 4 players and with unplugged pads.
Adds:

  runtime/ps2_host_pad.h   Ps2HostPad { user, port_count (<=2), slots_per_port[2] (<=4), read(user, port,
        slot, Ps2HostPadState*) } and Ps2HostPadState { connected, buttons (active low, layout of bytes
        2-3 of the pad buffer), rx/ry/lx/ly, has_pressure, pressure[12] in buffer-byte order 8..19 }.
  PS2Runtime::setHostPad(const Ps2HostPad*)   copies the struct; nullptr removes it. Call while the game
        thread is not running. The read callback runs on the game thread inside scePadRead / GetState /
        InfoMode / InfoPressMode / InfoAct and must only copy a state published by the host's own thread.
  PSPadBackend (ps2_pad.h/.cpp): setHostSource, setHostOwned (called by setHostOwnsWindow), hostMode,
        hasHostSource, hostSource, readHost, portCount, slotCount. "Host mode" = a source is installed OR
        the host owns the window. In host mode raylib is never called for input; without a source every
        pad is "not connected". Not in host mode (no source, runtime owns its window) the old raylib body
        is used unchanged (moved to readRaylibState), 2 ports, 1 slot.
  Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp: per (port, slot) state (was per port: slots collide with a multitap shape);
        scePadGetPortMax / scePadGetSlotMax(port) return the description; a (port, slot) outside it
        cannot be opened (scePadPortOpen returns 0); a pad that is not connected makes scePadRead return
        0 with the buffer filled as "disconnected" (byte 0 = 0xFF, buttons 0xFF 0xFF, sticks 0x80),
        scePadGetState 0, scePadInfoMode/InfoPressMode/InfoAct 0. Pressure bytes come from
        has_pressure/pressure[] when the source gives them (only after scePadEnterPressMode, as before),
        else 0 or 255 from the buttons as before. setPadHostTopology() carries the description from
        setHostPad into the Pad stubs.

raylib call sites of the pad code: ps2_pad.cpp readRaylibState (only when not in host mode),
Pad.cpp applyGamepadState / applyKeyboardState / findFirstGamepad (same), and the PS2_IF_AGRESSIVE_LOGS
trace in scePadRead (IsKeyDown, IsGamepadButtonDown; now skipped in host mode). Together with patch 0007
the runtime with a host-owned window calls no raylib function at all.

Assumption, not verified against hardware or a game: the byte values of the "disconnected" pad buffer.

How it was verified: tests/runtime/host_pad_source_test.cpp, with DISPLAY unset: a real PS2Runtime, the
pad handlers called as the generated code calls them. 2 ports x 2 slots each carrying its own buttons and
sticks; an unplugged pad (read 0, status 0xFF, GetState 0, InfoMode 0); ports/slots outside the
description cannot be opened; {4} (multitap shape) and the return to 2x1 after setHostPad(nullptr);
pressure bytes after scePadEnterPressMode; no source with a host-owned window = not connected and zero
raylib calls (recorders); legacy path (no source, own window) = connected, 2x1, raylib asked for keys.

Based on: original work for this project against PS2Recomp commit
2c5fbb9389e11dd95693385969490c9e8e6f57b4, on top of patches 0001 to 0006 and 0007.

